{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":25824456,"ns":0,"title":"Double suspension theorem","extract":"In geometric topology,  the double suspension theorem of James W. Cannon (Cannon (1979)) and Robert D. Edwards states that the double suspension S2X of a homology sphere X is a topological sphere.\nIf X is a piecewise-linear homology sphere but not a sphere, then its double suspension S2X (with a triangulation derived by applying the double suspension operation to a triangulation of X) is an example of a triangulation of a topological sphere that is not piecewise-linear.","description":"Theorem in geometric topology","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}